course: dictionary
lesson: 3343
title: Exact: completely correct
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exact means completely correct in every detail, not more or less. An exact answer is the right answer, not a guess or a rough estimate. If you round 19 up to 20, you have an estimate; 19 is the exact answer.
explain: Exact can also describe a person. Someone who is exact is careful and precise, and they notice every detail. You will often see it in phrases like the exact time, the exact copy, or the exact opposite. Try swapping in another word, such as correct or precise, to check that the meaning still fits.
explain: «Trainers use a whistle to say "yes, that's right" at the exact moment, then give a fish.» The whistle must come at the exact moment, not a second early or late, so the sea lion knows which action earned the fish. «"Cat123" is not the same password as "cat123".» Text checks are exact letter by letter, so one capital letter changes everything.
fact: Exact means completely correct, in every detail.
fact: «To be exact» means giving the precise detail, with nothing left out.
fact: An estimate is a rough guess close to the real amount; an exact answer is the real amount itself.
fact: «Nobody knows its exact birthday» means no one has the precise date, so a round date can be chosen instead.
fact: Exact can describe a person who is careful and precise.
exercise: «The exact time of the bus was 8:15, not 8:00.» What does exact mean here? | Roughly, about | *Completely correct, with no guessing | Late and noisy | Very large
exercise: What is the exact answer to 9 + 10? | Around 18 | About 20 | *19 | Nearly 20
exercise: Ella says exact is the same as roughly. Why is she wrong? | Roughly means very small | Roughly and exact both mean the same thing, so she is right | Exact means very large | *Exact means completely correct, but roughly means close, not perfect
test:
exam:
